/*!
@defgroup rtc
@ingroup mod_timer Real Time Clock (RTC)
@brief Calendar timekeeping, alarms, clock output, and periodic interrupt support.

@details
The RTC module provides a low-power hardware time base that tracks elapsed
seconds and exposes helper APIs for converting between the hardware seconds
counter and human-readable calendar values. The driver also supports alarm
scheduling, periodic seconds interrupts, time-drift compensation, and optional
clock-output routing.

@section rtc_features Key Features
- 32-bit RTC seconds counter with calendar conversion helpers.
- Calendar-based read/write APIs using `rtc_timedate_t`.
- One-shot and recurring alarm scheduling through `rtc_alarm_config_t`.
- Periodic seconds interrupt generation from 1 Hz up to 128 Hz.
- Overflow interrupt callback support.
- Programmable time compensation for RTC drift correction.
- Optional RTC clock-output routing to either the selected RTC clock source or
  the periodic seconds waveform.
- Support for devices with either shared or dedicated seconds IRQ lines.

@section rtc_modes Supported Modes

@subsection rtc_modes_seconds Periodic Seconds Interrupt Rates
| Configuration     | Interrupt Rate |
|-------------------|----------------|
| RTC_INT_1HZ       | 1 Hz           |
| RTC_INT_2HZ       | 2 Hz           |
| RTC_INT_4HZ       | 4 Hz           |
| RTC_INT_8HZ       | 8 Hz           |
| RTC_INT_16HZ      | 16 Hz          |
| RTC_INT_32HZ      | 32 Hz          |
| RTC_INT_64HZ      | 64 Hz          |
| RTC_INT_128HZ     | 128 Hz         |

@subsection rtc_modes_clkout Clock-Output Pin Modes
| Mode                  | Description                                           |
|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_CLKOUT_DISABLED   | Disable the RTC clock-output pin.                     |
| RTC_CLKOUT_SRC_SEC    | Output the periodic seconds interrupt waveform.       |
| RTC_CLKOUT_SRC_CLKSEL | Output the RTC clock selected by `rtc_clk_source_t`.  |

@subsection rtc_modes_clock Clock Source Selection
The `rtc_clk_source_t` enumeration is defined in the device feature header and
varies slightly by device family. Typical options include:
- `RTC_CLK_SRC_OSC_32KHZ`
- `RTC_CLK_SRC_RTC_PIN`
- `RTC_CLK_SRC_SIRC`
- `RTC_CLK_SRC_IPC`

@section rtc_arch Module Architecture

The RTC module is organized in a two-layer structure:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Application Code                │
│         (calls RTC_DRV_* functions)          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          RTC Driver Layer (rtc_driver.h/c)   │
│  ● Instance-based public API                 │
│  ● Calendar conversion and runtime state     │
│  ● Callback dispatch for alarm/overflow/sec  │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│    RTC HW Access Layer (rtc_hw_access.h/c)   │
│  ● Direct register programming helpers       │
│  ● Counter, alarm, compensation, IRQ bits    │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│             RTC Peripheral Hardware          │
│       (SEC, ALM, CMP, CTRL, INTE, INTF)      │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@section rtc_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection rtc_config_init rtc_init_config_t Fields
| Field                | Type                    | Description                                                  | Default |
|----------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|---------|
| compensationInterval | uint8_t                 | Compensation interval written to the RTC CMP register.       | 0       |
| compensation         | int8_t                  | Compensation value applied to the prescaler.                 | 0       |
| clockSource          | rtc_clk_source_t        | RTC clock source selected from the device feature header.    | First enum value |
| clockOutConfig       | rtc_clk_out_config_t    | RTC clock-output pin source selection.                       | RTC_CLKOUT_DISABLED |
| debugEnable          | bool                    | Keep RTC control accessible while debugging.                 | true    |
| rtcAlarmConfig       | rtc_alarm_config_t *    | Optional alarm configuration retained by the driver.         | Caller-defined |
| rtcOverflowConfig    | rtc_overflow_config_t * | Optional overflow interrupt configuration retained by driver.| Caller-defined |
| rtcSecondsConfig     | rtc_seconds_config_t *  | Optional periodic seconds interrupt configuration.           | Caller-defined |

@subsection rtc_config_alarm rtc_alarm_config_t Fields
| Field              | Type             | Description                                              | Default |
|--------------------|------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|---------|
| alarmTime          | rtc_timedate_t   | Absolute alarm target in calendar form.                  | Caller-defined |
| repetitionInterval | uint32_t         | Repeat interval, in seconds, for recurring alarms.       | 0       |
| numberOfRepeats    | uint32_t         | Remaining repeat count when `repeatForever` is false.    | 0       |
| repeatForever      | bool             | Keep rescheduling the alarm indefinitely.                | false   |
| alarmIntEnable     | bool             | Enable the hardware alarm interrupt source.              | false   |
| rtcAlarmCallback   | void (*)(void *) | Callback invoked from the alarm interrupt path.          | NULL    |
| callbackParams     | void *           | User context passed to `rtcAlarmCallback`.               | NULL    |

@subsection rtc_config_seconds rtc_seconds_config_t Fields
| Field              | Type                 | Description                                          | Default |
|--------------------|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------|---------|
| secondsIntConfig   | rtc_second_int_cfg_t | Periodic seconds interrupt frequency.                | Caller-defined |
| secondsIntEnable   | bool                 | Enable the periodic seconds interrupt source.        | false   |
| rtcSecondsCallback | void (*)(void *)     | Callback invoked from the seconds interrupt path.    | NULL    |
| callbackParams     | void *               | User context passed to `rtcSecondsCallback`.         | NULL    |

@subsection rtc_config_overflow rtc_overflow_config_t Fields
| Field               | Type             | Description                                          | Default |
|---------------------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------|---------|
| overflowIntEnable   | bool             | Enable the overflow interrupt source.                | false   |
| rtcOverflowCallback | void (*)(void *) | Callback invoked from the overflow interrupt path.   | NULL    |
| callbackParams      | void *           | User context passed to `rtcOverflowCallback`.        | NULL    |

@subsection rtc_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro                              | Description                                                  |
|------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_RTC_HAS_SEPARATE_SECOND_IRQ| Set to 1 when the device exposes a dedicated seconds IRQ.   |
| FEATURE_RTC_HAS_OSC                | Indicates support for the RTC 32.768 kHz oscillator source. |

@section rtc_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection rtc_usage_basic Pattern 1: Basic Initialization and Time Start-Up

@code{.c}
#define INST_RTC (0U)

static const rtc_timedate_t g_startTime =
{
    .year = 2026U,
    .month = 4U,
    .day = 4U,
    .hour = 9U,
    .minutes = 30U,
    .seconds = 0U
};

void RTC_BasicStart(void)
{
    rtc_init_config_t rtcConfig;

    RTC_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&rtcConfig);
    rtcConfig.clockSource = RTC_CLK_SRC_OSC_32KHZ;
    rtcConfig.clockOutConfig = RTC_CLKOUT_DISABLED;
    rtcConfig.rtcAlarmConfig = NULL;
    rtcConfig.rtcOverflowConfig = NULL;
    rtcConfig.rtcSecondsConfig = NULL;

    (void)RTC_DRV_Init(INST_RTC, &rtcConfig);
    (void)RTC_DRV_SetTimeDate(INST_RTC, &g_startTime);
    (void)RTC_DRV_StartCounter(INST_RTC);
}
@endcode

@subsection rtc_usage_seconds Pattern 2: Configure a Periodic Seconds Interrupt

@code{.c}
#define INST_RTC (0U)

static void RtcSecondsCallback(void *callbackParam)
{
    (void)callbackParam;
}

void RTC_EnableSecondsInterrupt(void)
{
    rtc_seconds_config_t secondsConfig =
    {
        .secondsIntConfig = RTC_INT_1HZ,
        .secondsIntEnable = true,
        .rtcSecondsCallback = RtcSecondsCallback,
        .callbackParams = NULL
    };

    RTC_DRV_ConfigureSecondsInt(INST_RTC, &secondsConfig);
}
@endcode

@subsection rtc_usage_alarm Pattern 3: Configure a Recurring Alarm

@code{.c}
#define INST_RTC (0U)

static void RtcAlarmCallback(void *callbackParam)
{
    (void)callbackParam;
}

void RTC_EnableRecurringAlarm(void)
{
    rtc_alarm_config_t alarmConfig =
    {
        .alarmTime =
        {
            .year = 2026U,
            .month = 4U,
            .day = 4U,
            .hour = 9U,
            .minutes = 31U,
            .seconds = 0U
        },
        .repetitionInterval = 60U,
        .numberOfRepeats = 10U,
        .repeatForever = false,
        .alarmIntEnable = true,
        .rtcAlarmCallback = RtcAlarmCallback,
        .callbackParams = NULL
    };

    (void)RTC_DRV_ConfigureAlarmInt(INST_RTC, &alarmConfig);
}
@endcode

@section rtc_api API Quick Reference

@subsection rtc_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function                    | Description                                                     |
|-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_Init()              | Initialize the RTC instance and store runtime callback state.   |
| RTC_DRV_Deinit()            | Reset the RTC instance with a software reset.                   |
| RTC_DRV_GetDefaultConfig()  | Fill the core initialization fields with driver defaults.       |

@subsection rtc_api_interrupt_ctrl Interrupt Source Control
| Function                         | Description                                          |
|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_SetRtcInterrupt()        | Enable one RTC interrupt source in hardware.         |
| RTC_DRV_ClearRtcInterrupt()      | Disable one RTC interrupt source in hardware.        |
| RTC_DRV_ClearRtcInterruptFlag()  | Clear one RTC interrupt status flag.                 |

@subsection rtc_api_time Counter Control and Time Access
| Function                         | Description                                          |
|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_StartCounter()           | Enable the RTC counter.                              |
| RTC_DRV_StopCounter()            | Disable the RTC counter.                             |
| RTC_DRV_GetCurrentTimeDate()     | Read the current RTC time in calendar form.          |
| RTC_DRV_SetTimeDate()            | Program the RTC time from a calendar value.          |

@subsection rtc_api_lock Register Protection
| Function                         | Description                                          |
|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_LockRegisters()          | Lock the RTC register interface for the instance.    |

@subsection rtc_api_comp Time Compensation
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_ConfigureTimeCompensation()   | Program RTC compensation interval and value.      |
| RTC_DRV_GetTimeCompensation()         | Read the active compensation interval and value.  |

@subsection rtc_api_callback Interrupt Callback Configuration
| Function                         | Description                                           |
|----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_ConfigureOverflowInt()   | Store overflow callback state and enable bit.         |
| RTC_DRV_ConfigureSecondsInt()    | Configure periodic seconds frequency and callback.    |

@subsection rtc_api_alarm Alarm Management
| Function                         | Description                                           |
|----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_ConfigureAlarmInt()      | Validate and program a one-shot or recurring alarm.   |
| RTC_DRV_GetAlarmConfig()         | Copy the alarm configuration currently stored.        |
| RTC_DRV_IsAlarmPending()         | Read the RTC alarm flag.                              |
| RTC_DRV_GetNextAlarmTime()       | Convert the next recurring alarm time to calendar form. |

@subsection rtc_api_convert Conversion & Validation Helpers
| Function                               | Description                                         |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_ConvertSecondsToTimeDate()     | Convert RTC seconds to calendar form.               |
| RTC_DRV_ConvertTimeDateToSeconds()     | Convert calendar form to RTC seconds.               |
| RTC_DRV_IsYearLeap()                   | Check whether a year is a leap year.                |
| RTC_DRV_IsTimeDateCorrectFormat()      | Validate an RTC calendar time value.                |

@subsection rtc_api_irq Internal IRQ Handlers
| Function                      | Description                                              |
|-------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| RTC_DRV_IRQHandler()          | Handle generic RTC alarm and overflow interrupt work.    |
| RTC_DRV_SecondsIRQHandler()   | Handle the periodic seconds interrupt.                   |

@section rtc_notes Important Notes

@subsection rtc_notes_clock Clock and Board Dependencies
- The RTC clock source is not configured by the driver. The application must
  select and enable the desired RTC source before calling RTC_DRV_Init().
- Clock-output pin muxing is also outside the driver. Configure board-level pin
  routing before expecting a waveform on the RTC clock-output pin.

@subsection rtc_notes_counter Counter State Requirements
- Call RTC_DRV_StopCounter() before RTC_DRV_SetTimeDate(); the write is rejected
  when the counter is still running.
- After a reset-state initialization flow, the counter remains disabled until
  RTC_DRV_StartCounter() is called.
- RTC_DRV_Deinit() returns `STATUS_ERROR` when the counter is already disabled.

@subsection rtc_notes_alarm Alarm Constraints
- RTC_DRV_ConfigureAlarmInt() accepts alarm times only when they are valid and
  strictly later than the current RTC time.
- Recurring-alarm rescheduling happens in RTC_DRV_IRQHandler(). If the alarm
  interrupt is not enabled or dispatched, the next alarm time is not refreshed.
- RTC_DRV_GetNextAlarmTime() is valid only after a recurring alarm has been
  rescheduled by the interrupt handler.

@subsection rtc_notes_config Initialization Defaults
- RTC_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() initializes only the core RTC fields. The optional
  pointer fields (`rtcAlarmConfig`, `rtcOverflowConfig`, `rtcSecondsConfig`)
  must be set explicitly by the caller before RTC_DRV_Init().

@subsection rtc_notes_irq Device IRQ Topology
- On devices where `FEATURE_RTC_HAS_SEPARATE_SECOND_IRQ == 0`, the generic RTC
  vector wrapper dispatches both RTC_DRV_IRQHandler() and
  RTC_DRV_SecondsIRQHandler().
- On devices with a dedicated seconds IRQ, the seconds callback runs from
  `RTC_Seconds_IRQHandler()`.

@section rtc_integration Integration Guide

@subsection rtc_integration_units Compilation Units
Compile the following files into the project:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/rtc/rtc_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/rtc/rtc_hw_access.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/rtc/rtc_irq.c
@endverbatim

@subsection rtc_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following include path to the toolchain:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection rtc_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No additional compile symbols are required for this component.

@subsection rtc_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager
- @ref interrupt_manager
*/
